{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Re-adding a model with incompatible settings can persist a configuration that prevents the daemon from starting after restart."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bare IPv6 SSH destination causes local management commands, including stop, to fail before contacting the host."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Resuming an interrupted mixed-target evaluation is rejected when one saved target has been retired."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Retrying a historical run is refused when its saved chain contains a retired model, even if a fallback remains available."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The current configuration wiring works, but the requested CLI-level configuration coverage is missing."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A provider whose endpoint does not match the documented host and port is not automatically managed, requiring an operator workaround."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Supplying an SSH option as the host can produce a misleading service status without contacting a server."},{"id":"C3b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A historical run retry is refused when its inherited model chain includes a retired target, despite an available fallback."}]}